{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"lumped capacity cooling of hot water lumped capacity cooling of hot water","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water.md","fileName":"Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Applied Thermal System Case Studies]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Applied Thermal System Case Studies","Axisymmetric Water and Spoon Model","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"lumped capacity cooling of hot water lumped capacity cooling of hot water","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water.md","fileName":"Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water","heading":"Lumped-Capacity Cooling of Hot Water","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A lumped-capacity model treats the water and immersed spoon as spatially uniform thermal masses that exchange heat through effective convection. Their transient temperatures depend on mass, specific heat, area, heat-transfer coefficient, and the initial difference from the surroundings.\n\nThe calculation provides a transparent benchmark for more detailed finite-element models. It captures overall equalization but cannot resolve internal circulation or local gradients, which motivates the later [[Axisymmetric Water and Spoon Model|axisymme